From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:30:48 -0643
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: describe Tensor G4's
 PMU clock

The Tensor G4 PMU (google,zumapro-pmu) gates the NFC controller's
reference clock pad, which clk-exynos-clkout provides like the Exynos
CLKOUT clocks. Say what #clock-cells numbers there: clock 0 is that pad.

Only the Pixel 9a's devicetree is known to use it, so this names Tensor
G4 rather than google,zuma-pmu in general.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
index 2f273e9e5..9cec4a137 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.yaml
@@ -63,6 +63,10 @@ properties:
 
   '#clock-cells':
     const: 1
+    description:
+      On the Exynos SoCs, one clock per CLKOUT mux input. On the Tensor G4
+      PMU (google,zumapro-pmu), clock 0 is the NFC controller's reference
+      clock pad.
 
   clock-names:
     description:
